SUMMARY:Seuls en Scène 2026 presents Nom by Constance Debré
LOCATION:Hearst Theater\, Lewis Arts Complex
DESCRIPTION:Hugues Jourdain and Victoria Quesnel have crafted a captivati
 ng production based on the novel\, Nom\, written by Constance Debré . I
 n her third book\, Debré pursues her relentless quest for freedom\, cha
 rting a new course in her struggle: how to love better? She casts off th
 e "corpses" haunting her life and abandons almost everything—family\, 
 marriage\, career—even contemplating the abolition of her lineage and 
 her family name. On a bare stage\, where only the power of words resonat
 es\, Victoria Quesnel—whose work in Julien Gosselin’s productions ha
 s drawn acclaim—makes this raw voice her own\, immersing the audience 
 in an unfiltered\, brilliant\, abrasive train of thought. Constance Debr
 é left her career as a lawyer to become a writer. She is the author of 
 a trilogy of novels: Playboy\, Love Me Tender\, and No Name (Nom) . This
  production marks the first time a text by Debré has been adapted for t
 he\nAudience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/
 seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-nom-constance-debre-0
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-no
 m-constance-debre-0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
