SUMMARY:Making Maps and Presentations using QGIS
LOCATION:Lewis Library - Computer Classroom (225)\, Lewis Science Library
DESCRIPTION:Maps can be extremely effective in communicating knowledge ab
 out an area. QGIS has many tools and techniques to design maps. Hands-on
  exercises will show how to use map-making tools within the software and
  introduce common cartographic techniques. The session will discuss how 
 to design maps for a variety of presentation formats. Attendees will use
  QGIS on classroom Windows computers. This event is part of the Geograph
 ic Information Systems (GIS) workshop series.\nAudience: Faculty & Acade
 mic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2
 026/making-maps-and-presentations-using-qgis
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/making-maps-and-presentations-u
 sing-qgis
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
