SUMMARY:Library Research for Uranium
LOCATION:Commons Large\, Hybrid Meeting Room (D312)\, Commons Library
DESCRIPTION:The Princeton University Library provides print and digital l
 ibrary sources from chemistry and geosciences collections specific to ch
 emical and geologic processes. This 30-minute introductory workshop will
  provide attendees with tips to finding library research for uranium iso
 topes\, decay chain\, source rocks\, aqueous solutions\, and uses in eme
 rging technologies. From 2008 to 2018\, Emily was the research librarian
  for the USGS Uranium Mineral Systems program https://www.usgs.gov/cente
 rs/central-energy-resources-science-center/science/uranium-mineral-syste
 ms#multimedia Emily’s Library Research Guides: Chemistry https://libgu
 ides.princeton.edu/chem Geosciences https://libguides.princeton.edu/geo\
 nAudience: Faculty & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://
 www.princeton.edu/events/2026/library-research-uranium-1
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/library-research-uranium-1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
