SUMMARY:Jane Street Guts++ at Princeton
LOCATION:Friend Center 006
DESCRIPTION:“Guts” was originally created as and remains a contest ro
 und of HMMT\, a math competition for high schoolers organized entirely b
 y Harvard and MIT students. There's a JS spin on it to create Guts++ - a
  fast-paced team game including a mix of math\, puzzles\, random trivia\
 , clever game theory and meta-level considerations.\nhttps://careerdevel
 opment.princeton.edu/events/jane-street-guts-princeton
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/jane-street-guts-princ
 eton
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4bd12899df7269d4207d040730ddb3cd
DTSTAMP:20260920T025819Z
DTSTART:20260921T220000Z
DTEND:20260921T230000Z
SUMMARY:Kenya’s Future: Democracy\, Leadership\, and the Next Generatio
 n: A Conversation with David Maraga
LOCATION:Louis A. Simpson International Building\, A71
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation with David Maraga\, former Chief J
 ustice and President of the Supreme Court of Kenya and a candidate in Ke
 nya’s 2027 presidential election. Hear directly from one of Kenya’s 
 most prominent political and judicial figures as he discusses the future
  of Kenya\, democracy\, leadership\, judicial independence\, elections\,
  accountability\, and youth participation. The conversation will be foll
 owed by an open student Q&A\, giving Princeton students the opportunity 
 to engage directly with Maraga and ask their own questions about Kenya
 ’s institutions\, challenges\, and future. Moderated by Professor Mahi
 ri Mwita.\nAudience: Open to the Public\, Faculty & Academic Professiona
 ls\, Students\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/kenyas-future-democ
 racy-leadership-and-next-generation-conversation-david-maraga
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/kenyas-future-democracy-leaders
 hip-and-next-generation-conversation-david-maraga
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
