LOCATION:Garden Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the U.S. premiere screening of De la Comédie-Fra
 nçaise by Martin Darondeau and Bertrand Usclat. The film depicts a nerv
 e-racking opening night for Nina\, who is directing Macbeth with her fel
 low troupe members. Nothing goes as planned before the curtains goes up.
  Critically praised\, the film is an uplifting homage to the theater pre
 sented by an impressive roster of current members of the Comédie-Franç
 aise playing an irresistible variety of roles. Guillaume Gallienne\, Ben
 jamin Laverhne\, Marina Hands\, Laurent Stocker\, Julien Frison\, Sépho
 ra Pondi\, Christian Hecq\, Florence Viala\, Françoise Gillard\, Serge 
 Bagdassarian\, Adeline d’Hermy\, and Danièle Lebrun\, among others\, 
 form the cast of the French comedy of the summer! The film stars Pauline
  Clément\, who first came to Seuls en Scène with Bertrand Usclat in 20
 15 to present Comme la lune. Post-Screening Discussion The screening wil
 l \nAudience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/
