UID:c0a5d13db39423560fba75026b115804
DTSTAMP:20260920T025617Z
DTSTART:20260922T203000Z
DTEND:20260922T213000Z
SUMMARY:Glyn Morgan Lecture
LOCATION:Aaron Burr Hall\, 219
DESCRIPTION:From early in the 1940s\, US policymakers started planning fo
 r Europe’s postwar order. The plan that emerged involved the creation 
 of a distinctively American Europe\, which included a federation of demo
 cratic states. While Europeans like to think that they were responsible 
 for the project of European integration\, they were largely executing a 
 plan that Americans had set in motion. American Europe has endured for r
 oughly 80 years. The current US administration is now seeking to dismant
 le this state-form and replace it with a new state form\, which I call C
 ivilizational America. This talk explains the rise and fall of American 
 Europe. It poses the question- what does non-domination require in a wor
 ld where a relatively benign hegemony has given way to predatory hegemon
 y?\nAudience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/
 glyn-morgan-lecture
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/glyn-morgan-lecture
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
