 mines how resilient the natural world can be – if we choose to protect
  it. The artist will speak about her work in the Briger Hall auditorium 
 at 4:30pm\, and be joined on stage by David Wilcove\, Henry W. Putnam Pr
 ofessor of Ecology and Evolutionary Biology and the High Meadows Institu
 te\; Professor of Public Affairs. Their conversation will be moderated b
 y Rachael DeLue\, Professor of American Art and Director of the Princeto
 n Humanities Initiative. At the conclusion of the program\, the exhibiti
 on will open in the Environmental Gallery and Briger Hall atrium. Free a
 nd open to the public. Persons planning to attend are encouraged to regi
 ster here. Please note registration does not guarantee a seat\nAudience:
