SUMMARY:Opening event: "Real and Remembered: Princetonians Caught between
  Study and Revolution"
LOCATION:Mudd Manuscript Library\, Mudd Manuscript Library
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the public opening of "Real and Remembered: Princ
 etonians Caught between Study and Revolution." Even before the American 
 Revolution directly impacted campus life–with Nassau Hall occupied\, c
 lasses disrupted\, and students leaving to fight–Princeton had become 
 a center of revolutionary thought and youthful activism. The Revolution 
 was a key part of institutional identity and school spirit. This exhibit
 ion highlights both the real and remembered Revolution at Princeton\, 25
 0 years later. Curated by Library Collections Specialists\, April C. Arm
 strong *14\, Ashley Augustyniak\, and Rosalba Varallo Recchia. A pop-up 
 exhibit with additional related items will be on display. Light snacks w
 ill be available. To help us anticipate attendance\, registration (below
 ) is requested.\nAudience: Faculty & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, St
 udents\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/opening-event-real-and-rem
 embered-princetonians-caught-between-study-and-revolution
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/opening-event-real-and-remember
 ed-princetonians-caught-between-study-and-revolution
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
