SUMMARY:Curator Talk | Intimate Grief: Death in Ancient Greece
LOCATION:Art Museum\, 100 Grand Hall
DESCRIPTION:A curatorial discussion of funerary objects and rituals in an
 cient Greece In this talk\, Carolyn Laferrière\, curator of ancient Med
 iterranean art\, and Nathan Arrington\, professor and chair of the Depar
 tment of Art & Archaeology and Hellenic Studies\, will discuss how mortu
 ary objects in ancient Greece could establish intimate connections betwe
 en the living and the dead\, allowing mourners to approach the deceased 
 once again—if only in the mind—and to form communities of remembranc
 e. The talk is presented in advance of a special exhibition focusing on 
 the more personal aspects of mourning\, opening Fall 2028. Cosponsored b
 y the Department of Art and Archeology\, the Department of Classics\, an
 d the Princeton University Art Museum.\nAudience: Open to the Public\, F
 aculty & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\, Alumni\nhttps://www
 .princeton.edu/events/2026/curator-talk-intimate-grief-death-ancient-gre
 ece
