SUMMARY:The Endless Frontier - Documentary Screening & Panel
LOCATION:Briger Hall\, C112 Lecture Hall
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Briger Hall Auditorium on September 24th at 6:30 P
 M to watch The Endless Frontier\, a new documentary film featuring Princ
 eton's own Dr. Andrea Graham! The film is an intimate\, urgent portrait 
 of three scientists working to solve some of the most pressing challenge
 s of our time\, from disease to climate change\, while revealing the gro
 wing threat to the American research engine and what is at stake for us 
 all if it falters. You can watch the trailer here. The film will be foll
 owed by a panel discussion between Prof. Graham\, director Marilyn Ness\
 , and producer Beth Westrate. The panel will be moderated by Prof. Heath
 er Howard of SPIA. This event is made possible by the Department of Ecol
 ogy and Evolutionary Biology in partnership with the Center for Health a
 nd Wellbeing.\nAudience: Open to the Public\, Faculty & Academic Profess
 ionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/endless
 -frontier-documentary-screening-panel
