SUMMARY:Career Essentials: Interview with Confidence
LOCATION:Frist Campus Center\, Class of 1952 Room (A Leve
DESCRIPTION:Interviews are more than a chance to answer questions. They a
 re an opportunity to communicate your experience\, demonstrate your stre
 ngths and show why you are a strong fit for an organization. This worksh
 op is designed to help students prepare effectively and develop the conf
 idence needed to succeed in a variety of interview settings and situatio
 ns. In this workshop\, you will learn: 1. Different purposes and stages 
 of interviewing 2. Common types of interview questions and how to approa
 ch them 3. How to create a strong first impression and express compatibi
 lity for a position 4. How to develop behavioral interview stories using
  the STAR method 5. Best practices for virtual and in-person interviews 
 This program is open to all Princeton University undergraduates regardle
 ss of identity. Email [careerdevelopment@princeton.edu](mailto:careerdev
 elopment@princeton.edu) to request accommodations\nRegister: https://app
 .joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1977078\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princet
 on.edu/events/career-essentials-interview-confidence
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/career-essentials-inte
 rview-confidence
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
