SUMMARY:Seuls en Scène 2026 presents Génération Mitterand – Huit roi
 s (nos présidents)\, Episode 2 by Léo Cohen-Paperman & Émilien Diard-
 Detoeuf
LOCATION:Whitman College
DESCRIPTION:Marie-France is a journalist in Paris\, Luc is a teacher in V
 énissieux\, and Michel is a factory worker in Belfort. At eighteen\, th
 ey lived through the events of May '68. In 1981\, they voted for Franço
 is Mitterrand. Then\, in 2022\, they voted for Emmanuel Macron\, Jean-Lu
 c Mélenchon\, and Marine Le Pen\, respectively. To understand why they 
 no longer agree on anything—and can no longer stand one another—they
  take turns playing "their" president. Génération Mitterrand is the se
 cond installment in the series Huit rois (nos présidents) . These deepl
 y personal presidential portraits examine French society\, looking at bo
 th those who shape it and those who live in it. At once tender\, funny\,
  and insightful\, this second episode dramatizes the hopes and disillusi
 onments of an entire generation. Writing a show about François Mitterra
 nd means writing a show about my parents’ generation—born after Worl
 d W\nAudience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026
 /seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-generation-mitterand-huit-rois-nos-preside
 nts-episode-2
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-ge
 neration-mitterand-huit-rois-nos-presidents-episode-2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
