SUMMARY:Seuls en Scène 2026 presents Losing Your Bag by Pascal Rambert
LOCATION:Blair Arch
DESCRIPTION:Postponed to 2027 . This work-in-progress one-woman piece is 
 a collaboration between renowned French playwright Pascal Rambert and ac
 tress Pauline Chalamet. The play follows a young woman with a master’s
  degree who is—temporarily—a window cleaner. Over the course of the 
 performance\, she expresses her anger at social stratification and grapp
 les with loneliness in a world divided between “people who succeed and
  people who are nothing.” Losing Your Bag comes to Princeton before ma
 king its English-language premiere at L’Alliance New York’s Crossing
  the Line Festival in November. Rambert\, who was a Visiting Belknap Fel
 low in the Council of the Humanities and Visiting Lecturer at Princeton 
 University\, returns to Seuls en Scène for the eighth time this year. 
 “A gritty text in which a window cleaner settles her scores with capit
 alist society.” —Le Monde Presented in collaboration with L’Allian
 ce\nAudience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/
 seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-losing-your-bag-pascal-rambert
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-lo
 sing-your-bag-pascal-rambert
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
