SUMMARY:Finding the Best Location using QGIS
LOCATION:Lewis Library - Computer Classroom (225)\, Lewis Science Library
DESCRIPTION:GIS (geographic information system) software allows the user 
 to treat the Earth’s surface as a continuous array of numbers. Images 
 and raster datasets can be used to rank suitable locations\, estimate ch
 ange\, and display phenomena such as elevation\, precipitation\, or temp
 erature. The session uses percent impervious surface\, distance from str
 eams\, and slope to assign each parameter a scale from 1 to 9\, and weig
 ht the relative suitability of different areas. This ‘weighted overlay
 ’ method is useful in a variety of contexts. The QGIS Python console a
 nd editor will be used to help build a Python script to process data. At
 tendees will use QGIS installed on classroom computers. This event is pa
 rt of the Geographic Information Systems (GIS) workshop series.\nAudienc
 e: Faculty & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.prin
 ceton.edu/events/2026/finding-best-location-using-qgis
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/finding-best-location-using-qgi
 s
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
