SUMMARY:Graduate School Application Essay Workshop
LOCATION:Center for Career Development\, Conference Room
DESCRIPTION:Graduate school application essays vary widely. Designed for 
 students and recent alumni actively applying to a master’s or Ph.D. pr
 ogram this year\, this session will help you get started with an individ
 ualized approach to your specific essays. We will analyze samples to und
 erstand key essay components\, inventory your background to identify you
 r alignment with programs and prioritize your writing to communicate you
 r fit as an applicant. By the end of this session\, you will have an out
 line of paragraphs for one of your essays. It is strongly suggested to b
 ring an essay prompt from your applications (drafts for essays are not n
 eeded). Both in-person and virtual attendance options are available for 
 this hybrid workshop. This program is open to all Princeton University u
 ndergraduates\, graduate students\, and recent alumni regardless of iden
 tity. Email [careerdevelopment@princeton.edu](mailto:c\nAudience: Alumni
 \, Graduate Students\, Undergraduate Students\nRegister: https://princet
 on.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1978248\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princ
 eton.edu/events/graduate-school-application-essay-workshop
