SUMMARY:iASpace — Interaural Space
LOCATION:CoLab\, Lewis Arts Complex
DESCRIPTION:iASpace is where sound\, bodies\, and presence come together\
 ; an experiment in collective attention. It is an invitation to what is 
 possible when listening is treated as a public resource\, and when a spa
 ce is dedicated to holding opacity rather than resolution. For seven day
 s\, the CoLab is transformed into a public space to stay\, listen\, retu
 rn\, and experience sound together. Schedule of Live Sound Works: 9/29 a
 t 5 PM — Sound performance with Leo Chang 10/1 at 6 PM — Somatic Res
 onance: Sound & Reiki workshop with Nanse & Bryce 10/3 at 2 PM — Synth
  Youth workshop with Sydney Spann 10/4 at 11 AM — Drone Decompression 
 with Beth Meyers The Listening Environment iASpace is a living instrumen
 t shaped through sound\, attention\, and collective presence. From 10 AM
 –8 PM each day\, the intentionally designed hi-fi room will continuous
 ly hold sound works by independent artists\, sound practitioners\, and\n
 Audience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/iasp
 ace-interaural-space-2
