SUMMARY:Using Tables and Maps together in QGIS
LOCATION:Lewis Library - Computer Classroom (225)\, Lewis Science Library
DESCRIPTION:U.S. Census data can be integrated with GIS (geographic infor
 mation system) boundary files to analyze the spatial relationships of po
 verty\, ethnicity\, environmental risk\, and other parameters. We will f
 ind and download demographic data\, combine the data with GIS files\, an
 d view the data in QGIS. The QGIS Python console and editor will be used
  to build a Python script to process data. The session will help any GIS
  user to include tabular data in spatial analyses. Attendees will use QG
 IS on the classroom Windows computers. This event is part of the Geograp
 hic Information Systems (GIS) workshop series.\nAudience: Faculty & Acad
 emic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/
