SUMMARY:Brentano String Quartet (Princeton University Concerts)
LOCATION:Richardson Auditorium\, Alexander Hall
DESCRIPTION:We open Princeton University Concerts’ 133rd Concert Classi
 cs Series with a dream come true: the beloved Brentano String Quartet\, 
 returning to their former home stage (1999–2014) for an evening of qui
 et wonder. Haydn’s “The Dream” flits between wit and reverie\; Jos
 ef Suk’s Meditation on an Old Czech Hymn draws on a melody centuries o
 ld\, transforming a prayer for protection into music of profound warmth 
 and hope\; Pēteris Vasks’s Meditation from his Fourth Quartet (2000) 
 offers a searching reflection on our modern world at the dawn of the 21s
 t century\; and Beethoven’s Quartet in E Minor\, Op. 59\, No. 2 closes
  with a slow movement that gazes\, rapt and awestruck\, at the starry fi
 rmament—inviting us to do the same as we begin another season of music
  together. Musicians Mark Steinberg & Serena Canin Violins Misha Amory V
 iola Nina Lee Cello This event is presented by Princeton University Conc
 ert\nAudience: Open to the Public\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026
 /brentano-string-quartet-princeton-university-concerts
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/brentano-string-quartet-princet
 on-university-concerts
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
