SUMMARY:Hip-Hop Techniques and Foundations with ESkilllz
LOCATION:Ellie's Studio\, Lewis Arts Complex
DESCRIPTION:This drop-in dance class series \, curated by dance program a
 lum Liam Lynch ’21 and taught on October 3\, 10 & 31 by guest artist E
 lijah “ESkilllz” Carr\, develops a diverse understanding of foundati
 onal techniques in street and club dance. With an emphasis on physical t
 echniques\, the class exposes dancers to a multitude of dance styles inc
 luding hip-hop\, house\, and popping. Through the sessions\, students wi
 ll understand the basic techniques of street dance and will also be chal
 lenged to synthesize elements of groove\, musicality\, texture\, footwor
 k\, and personal expression in their own individual improvisation. About
  ESkilllz Elijah “Eskilllz” Carr is a Jersey native and experienced 
 JERZ-style dance veteran. With a background in performance art\, he is k
 nown for his expressive and energetic approach to the evolving style. Es
 killlz specializes in musicality\, JERZ footwork\, and dynamic movement\
 nAudience: Faculty & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\, Alumni\
 nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/hip-hop-techniques-and-foundation
 s-eskilllz
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/hip-hop-techniques-and-foundati
 ons-eskilllz
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
