SUMMARY:Feeding the Arts with Catherine Barnett ’82
LOCATION:New South Building
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an informal career conversation over dinner with 
 award-winning poet and NYU professor Catherine Barnett ‘82. Catherine 
 will share some of her poetry\, speak about the life of a published poet
 \, and answer questions students may have about pursuing graduate studie
 s in creative writing. Dinner provided. About Catherine Barnett Barnett 
 is the author of four poetry collections\, including Solutions for the P
 roblem of Bodies in Space\; Human Hours\; The Game of Boxes \, and Into 
 Perfect Spheres Such Holes Are Pierced. A Guggenheim Fellow\, she receiv
 ed an Arts and Letters Award in Literature from the American Academy of 
 Arts and Letters\, teaches in NYU’s MFA Program in Creative Writing\, 
 and works as an independent editor. Admission Open to current students. 
 Advanced registration through Handshake required. Register via Handshake
  Directions Get directions to the creative writing Library \,\nAudience:
  Students\nRegister: https://princeton.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/2023
 847\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/feeding-arts-catherine-barnet
 t-82
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/feeding-arts-catherine-barnett-
 82
