SUMMARY:Responsible AI: Gathering Research Materials from the Internet
LOCATION:Commons Library Classroom (D112)\, Commons Library
DESCRIPTION:We'll cover practical methods for collecting secondary resear
 ch materials from the web\, along with the judgment calls that determine
  whether a collection is usable and defensible: what you have permission
  to gather\, how to handle privacy\, confidentiality\, and data sovereig
 nty\, and how to document consent and provenance as you go. We'll also p
 ractice recognizing when it's faster and more reliable to consult docume
 ntation or ask a direct question than to hand a task to a language model
 . Participants will come away with a repeatable\, responsible workflow f
 or turning scattered web sources into a defensible starting point for a 
 research dataset — plus a checklist of the privacy and provenance ques
 tions to ask before any material goes into their own collection.\nAudien
 ce: Faculty & Academic Professionals\, Staff\, Students\nhttps://www.pri
 nceton.edu/events/2026/responsible-ai-gathering-research-materials-inter
 net
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/responsible-ai-gathering-resear
 ch-materials-internet
